     3,
     "<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, June 15, 2023 at 2:51:09 PM UTC-6 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">murray...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">That&#39;s a good link. Also note the new functions chat.nk() and adjustvarD in &#39;secr&#39; (for straightforward SECR models, not mark-resight). Expect more developments in this area.<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Friday, June 16, 2023 at 4:01:38 AM UTC+12 <a rel=\"nofollow\">shane...@state.co.us</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"auto\">You can check out this one:</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\"><div><a href=\"https://bioone.org/journals/wildlife-biology/volume-2020/issue-1/wlb.00649/Consequences-of-ignoring-group-association-in-spatial-capturerecapture-analysis/10.2981/wlb.00649.full\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bioone.org/journals/wildlife-biology/volume-2020/issue-1/wlb.00649/Consequences-of-ignoring-group-association-in-spatial-capturerecapture-analysis/10.2981/wlb.00649.full&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486473122000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2x9SOdJGVkIZz9ENICDQy_\">https://bioone.org/journals/wildlife-biology/volume-2020/issue-1/wlb.00649/Consequences-of-ignoring-group-association-in-spatial-capturerecapture-analysis/10.2981/wlb.00649.full</a></div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><br></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Jun 15, 2023 at 09:54 Devin Fitzpatrick &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">devin...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\">Hello,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;min-height:15px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\">I am planning to estimate density using SMR of a species that travels in groups. I believe this grouping behaviour violates the model assumptions. Does anyone have any recommendations of resources on how to deal with this? Is it possible to account for during the analysis stage?</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;min-height:15px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\">Thank you,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\">Devin </p>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;secr&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">secrgroup+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web, visit <a href=\"https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__groups.google.com_d_msgid_secrgroup_e2e3f264-2Dabaa-2D47c4-2D92ec-2Dc9ee5c4fd209n-2540googlegroups.com-3Futm-5Fmedium-3Demail-26utm-5Fso